---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../data/site';

const effectiveDate = 'Effective August 9, 2026';
---

<LegalLayout title="Privacy policy | CareCache" description="How CareCache keeps home medical supply and device records local and under your control." heading="Privacy, without fine-print theater." intro="CareCache is designed to organize sensitive care information without sending that information to Vector42." effectiveDate={effectiveDate}>
  <nav slot="contents"><a href="#scope">Scope</a><a href="#collection">What we collect</a><a href="#local">Data on your device</a><a href="#leaves">When data leaves</a><a href="#permissions">Permissions</a><a href="#retention">Retention</a><a href="#security">Security</a><a href="#changes">Changes</a></nav>
  <section id="scope"><h2>Scope</h2><p>This policy applies to the CareCache iOS and Android application and this public website. CareCache is published by {siteConfig.publisher}.</p><p>CareCache is an organizational and reminder tool. It is not a medical device, clinical service, diagnostic tool, or emergency service.</p></section>
  <section id="collection"><h2>What Vector42 collects</h2><p>Vector42 collects no CareCache app records. The app has no account, Vector42 backend, advertising, analytics, crash-reporting SDK, remote logging, or behavioral tracking.</p><p>This website has no analytics, ads, account system, tracking pixels, or nonessential cookies. The hosting provider processes ordinary request information such as IP addresses and browser headers to deliver the site under its own terms.</p></section>
  <section id="local"><h2>Data kept on your device</h2><p>CareCache uses local SQLite storage and app-managed files. Depending on what you enter, records can include supply names and quantities; barcodes, lot numbers, expiration dates, and storage locations; cleaning and replacement history; device manufacturer, model, and serial number; supplier and warranty notes; user-entered prescription or setup reference fields; recognized label text; and app preferences.</p><p>CareCache does not send these records to Vector42 during ordinary use.</p></section>
  <section id="leaves"><h2>When information leaves the app</h2><p>Information leaves only through an action you take: exporting a <code>.carecache</code> backup through the system share sheet, selecting a destination such as local storage or an installed cloud file provider, or opening a supplier, manual, support, privacy, or terms link in another app.</p><p>The receiving person, browser, storage provider, or other service applies its own privacy and security practices. CareCache does not receive your cloud-provider credentials or a copy of the backup.</p></section>
  <section id="permissions"><h2>Optional device permissions</h2><ul><li>Camera access scans barcodes and captures a label for on-device text recognition.</li><li>Notifications support care reminders created by you.</li><li>File and share access supports backup export and restore through operating-system surfaces.</li></ul><p>Denying a permission limits only that feature. Manual entry and the rest of the local app remain available.</p></section>
  <section id="retention"><h2>Retention and deletion</h2><p>You control live records inside the app. Archived records can remain in local history and backups. Uninstalling CareCache removes local app data according to the operating system. Exported files remain wherever you saved or shared them until you remove them there.</p></section>
  <section id="security"><h2>Security and backups</h2><p>CareCache validates backup structure, checksums, identifiers, and relationships before changing live data, then restores in one database transaction. A local safety snapshot is created before a valid restore.</p><p>A <code>.carecache</code> backup is not encrypted by the app in version 1. Protect it with a device passcode, trusted destination, full-disk encryption, and any controls offered by your storage provider.</p></section>
  <section id="changes"><h2>Changes and contact</h2><p>If CareCache data practices change, this policy and the public repository privacy boundary will be updated before release, and the effective date above will change. Use the <a href="/support/">support page</a> for questions. Never include real medical information, serial numbers, barcodes, prescription details, or backup files in a public issue.</p></section>
</LegalLayout>
